==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἐμφατικός||emphatic|tr=emphatikos|lang=grc}} < {{etyl|grc}} {{term|lang=grc|ἔμφασις|tr=emphasis}} (English {{term|emphasis|lang=en}}), from {{term|ἐμφαίνω||I show, present|tr=emphainō|lang=grc}} from {{term|ἐν||in|tr=en|lang=grc}} + {{term|φαίνω||I shine, show|tr=phainō|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪmˈfætɪk/}}, {{SAMPA|/Im-fatik/}}
* {{rhymes|ætɪk}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by [[emphasis]].
# Stated with [[conviction]].
#: ''He gave me an '''emphatic''' no when I asked him out.''
# belonging to set of English tense forms comprising the auxiliary verb [[do]] + an infinitive without [[to]]
# {{phonology}} of [[obstruent]] [[consonant|consonants]] in [[Semitic]] languages.

